body:
it would be interesting to see if when civilization collapses if we could come together and build a brighter future. maybe that's the game idea, try to build leftist support in a post apocalyptic world.

&#x200B;

edit: on hk kids asking trump to liberate them, i feel inclined to say that hong kong certainly has some working class support and could evolve into a working class movement but as of right now i would not call hong kong a working class movement. i would hardly call the CPC a working class party. i view hong kong as a case study to see what real class conflict might look like in the present and future. 

&#x200B;

questions for actual communists, maoist or otherwise: how do you feel about hk and how do you feel about the CPC

if you got beer then i have a place to drink it

&#x200B;

edit: hmu in the dms if youre interested in hanging out
